{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095591-resources-for-bygones","id":1095591,"title":"Resources for Bygones?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-22T12:29:53-07:00","id":1095591,"title":"Resources for Bygones?","content":"Can anyone help me with this, I am searching for more info on bygones besides the Bygone Bestiary. While it covers many bygones, were there any others? Searching for creatures from the east besides lumping them into the category of spirits or chimera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T15:36:19-07:00","id":1095636,"title":"","content":"With the exception of the moth-man and one or two others in the revised edition Storyteller Screen companion book and one or two in Dragons of the East, I can't recall any others. M20 may have more, but I wouldn't know. <br /> <br /> If you're just needing ideas of real world Asian creatures of myth and legend instead of fully stat-ed out ones, Hero Games makes a pair of Asian Bestiary books for their 5th ed Fantasy Hero line that cover a fairly wide range of cultures. And my current go-to guide for mythological creatures is the Element Encyclopedia of Magical Creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T17:27:22-07:00","id":1095676,"title":"","content":"For almost all mythical creatures in my CWOD games I go to Google. Especially in Mage where its so easy to get a good gauge of their power level compared to the players simply by looking at their supernatural abilities and determining what spheres and at what levels would be required to duplicate the ability.<br /> <br /> Also NWOD / CoD has many interesting creatures spread over the line and they are fairly easy to convert to the CWOD format.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T18:14:14-07:00","id":1095695,"title":"","content":"I think the Books of Madness have sections on Umbrood and similar beings. Since summoning bygones is a fairly common Marauder effect, it might be helpful to look there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"tha